QuestGuidance.Register("en",255,{
[8129]="70026586\n1\tLook to the horizon\030Find a place to look over Lake Evendim\tOrchalwë spoke of spending time by the shore looking to the far horizon.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will want to hear what you thought while looking to the horizon.\n",
[8130]="70043E00\n1\tPatrol the Southern docks\030Patrol the central docks\030Patrol the central lookout\030Patrol the bridge to the Dome of Stars\030Patrol of overlook of the Northern courtyard\030Patrol the central courtyard\tPatrol the Eastern side of Osgiliath.\n2\tListen to Shíktarb yell at you\tShíktarb is at Shrak Mauruk. You should listen to Shíktarb yell at you.\n",
[8131]="70039E80\n1\tTalk to Selethryth\tSelethryth is located north-west of the Mead Hall. Thane Sparhafoc wants you to speak with the people of Fenmarch to see if they have any information about the Orcs or their encampment. You should begin with Selethryth.\n2\tTalk to Frethi\tFurther west of the Mead Hall, you will find Frethi. Thane Sparhafoc wants you to speak with the people of Fenmarch to see if they have any information about the Orcs.\n3\tTalk to Drytwald\tDrytwald can be found further west from Frethi. Thane Sparhafoc wants you to speak with the people of Fenmarch to see if they have any information regarding the Orcs. You should continue talking with the people of Fenmarch.\n4\tTalk to Tova\tTova is near the entrance to Fenmarch, to the west. Drytwald mentioned that Tova had recently seen a giant boar. You should speak with her.\n5\tTalk to Thane Sparhafoc\tAfter speaking with the people of Fenmarch, you found no evidence of Orcs, however this boar-skull totem might be worth examining. You should return to Thane Sparhafoc and let him know your findings.\n",
[8132]="7003FF79\n1\tSearch houses (total: 10)\tThe houses should be searched for corsairs.\n",
[8133]="70041358\n1\tFind the lost dog\tPebble the dog can be found somewhere within the village of Gaerlond.\n2\tAid the lost dog\tYou have come across Pebble the dog and should now aid her in returning to her master.\n3\tSpeak to Balangyl\tBalangyl can be found near the village of Gaerlond. You should speak with Balangyl.\n",
[8134]="700659CA\n1\tTalk to Eithriel\030Talk to Raithgam\030Talk to Brechan\tBerion has asked you to speak with some tradespeople on his behalf. Talk to tradespeople in Ost Anglebed.\n2\tTalk to Berion\tYou have spoken with the tradespeople only to learn that none can take on an apprentice. You'll have to deliver the bad news to Berion. Talk to Berion in Ost Anglebed.\n",
[8135]="7004D70B\n1\tTalk to the Master of Lake-town\tDagrun, Master of Lake-town, can be found in the Master's Manor in Lake-town. Suspicious that Karazgar's agents might still lurk in Lake-town, King Thorin III has asked you to seek an audience with the Master of Lake-town.\n2\tExamine suspicious cargo in Lake-town (total: 6) Suspicious cargo can only be found at night.\tSuspicious cargo can be found on and near the rowboats docked in Lake-town at night. Dagrun, Master of Lake-town, has asked you to investigate suspicious activity occurring at night in Lake-town. She believes that smugglers have been attempting to ferry illicit goods from Lake-town to forces of the Enemy.\n3\tSearch for more signs of foul play in Lake-town\tSigns of foul play might be found on the docks of Lake-town. You have uncovered the grisly remains of numerous cold-drakelings in Lake-town, but you are uncertain why they have been slain. You should continue your search for Karazgar's agents amongst the docks of Lake-town.\n4\tFollow the trail of blood through Lake-town\tDroplets of blood can be found snaking through eastern Lake-town. You have discovered a poorly-concealed trail of blood leading through Lake-town. You should follow it and see if it leads to Karazgar's agents.\n5\tApproach the window and listen closely to the voices within the old smugglers' den\tThe old smugglers' den can be found in the easternmost section of Lake-town. You have followed a trail of blood to the old smugglers' den in Lake-town, and you hear the voices of what can only be two of Karazgar's agents within. You should listen to their conversation before returning to the Master of Lake-town.\n6\tInform the Master of Lake-town of the Weeping Warrior's plot\tDagrun, Master of Lake-town, can be found in the Master's Manor in Lake-town. You have uncovered a curious plot by Karazgar to obtain the bodies of numerous cold-drakelings, and you have also learned that Karazgar has departed the Dale-lands for the realm of Eryn Lasgalen. You should inform the Master of Lake-town of what you have discovered.\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found in Erebor. You have discovered Karazgar's activities in Lake-town and learned that the Weeping Warrior has passed into Eryn Lasgalen. You should return to King Thorin III at once.\n",
[8136]="7004E4F5\n1\tTalk to Tuhâl\tYou should talk to Tuhâl, who can be found in Utterby.\n2\t'Threaten' shackled Easterlings (total: 6)\tShackled Easterlings can be found inside Utterby. You should secretly loosen the shackles of these Easterlings.\n3\tTalk to Yólkhon\tYou should talk to Yólkhon, can be found inside Utterby.\n",
[8137]="70071613\n1\tCollect stolen valuables (total: 15)\tKûrmi has asked you to retrieve the items stolen from the Beltáni. You should travel to the robber camp, Kidu-bâla, and retrieve the stolen valuables.\n2\tTalk to Kûrmi\tYou have reclaimed many items stolen by the robbers. You should return to Kûrmi in Ahâba with the items.\n",
[8138]="70037C88\n1\tDefeat Dunlending looters (total: 8)\tDunlending looters can be found rummaging around near the bodies of the fallen Rohirrim at the Fords of Isen. You should drive off Dunlending looters.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have driven off a number of Dunlending looters for the sake of the fallen Rohirrim at the Fords of Isen.\n",
[8139]="7001BE8C\n1\tCollect crates of stolen belongings at Bolg Maufulug (total: 7)\tBolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol. Faelleron has asked you to enter Bolg Maufulug and collect any stolen belongings you find there.\n2\tBring stolen belongings to Faelleron at Talan Fanuidhol\tFaelleron is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug. You should return to Faelleron with the stolen belongings you recovered.\n",
[8140]="7001BE8D\n1\tCollect crates of stolen belongings at Drûmaudhul (total: 12)\tDrûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith. Maeriel has asked you to enter Drûmaudhul and collect any stolen belongings you find there.\n2\tBring stolen belongings to Maeriel at Talan Gwilith\tMaeriel is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Drûmaudhul. You should return to Maeriel with the stolen belongings you recovered.\n",
[8141]="7002C765\n1\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (0/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n2\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (1/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n3\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (2/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n4\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (3/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n5\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (4/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n6\tUnlock Orc lockboxes and collect the treasure within (5/6)\tOrc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad. You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.\n7\tBring the Elf-treasure to Renfaer\tRenfaer, the scout of southern Thinglad, awaits you at his watch-post. You should bring the treasure you gathered to Renfaer.\n",
[8142]="7001BE8E\n1\tCollect crates of stolen belongings at Mokûrz Gundul (total: 7)\tMokûrz Gundul lies to the north-west from Talan Fanuidhol. Faelleron has asked you to enter Mokûrz Gundul and collect any stolen belongings you find there.\n2\tBring the stolen belongings to Faelleron at Talan Fanuidhol\tFaelleron is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul. You should return to Faelleron with the stolen belongings you recovered.\n",
[8143]="7001BE8F\n1\tCollect crates of stolen belongings at Nardur-stazg (total: 7)\tNardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith. Maeriel has asked you to enter Nardur-stazg and collect any stolen belongings you find there.\n2\tBring the stolen belongings to Maeriel at Talan Gwilith\tMaeriel is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg. You should return to Maeriel with the stolen belongings you recovered.\n",
[8144]="7006EBE6\n1\tSteal gold from Ekhamâti camp (total: 8)\030Defeat Omurtóko\030Defeat Khisónto\030Defeat Purombóro\tYour mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.\n2\tEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive\tEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[8145]="70040003\n1\tDefeat looters (total: 4)\tThe looters must be defeated and the weapons and armour secured.\n",
[8146]="70019D2F\n1\tTalk to Lady Galadriel in the House of Celeborn\030Talk to Lord Celeborn in the House of Celeborn\tLord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel can be found outside their house, high atop the greatest mallorn in Lothlórien. The carpeted path near Forbad winds up to the flet beneath the House of Celeborn. Forbad has recommended that you speak with Celeborn and Galadriel and to take advantage of the opportunity to see the view from the top.\n2\tTalk to Forbad at the base of the carpeted path beneath the House of Celeborn\tForbad is at the base of the carpeted path that climbs the mallorn to the House of Celeborn. You have spoken with Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel and should now return to Forbad.\n",
[8147]="7001CCD8\n1\tDefeat Agonglok at Fállug\tAgonglok may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angeled. Thindiel has asked you to defeat the Warg Agonglok.\n2\tTalk to Thindiel atop Amon Angened\tThindiel is at the way-post atop Amon Angeled, east of Fállug. You should bring news of your victory against Agonglok to Thindiel.\n",
[8148]="700001B0\n1\tDefeat Barashal\tBarashal is at Carn Dûm, to the west of Tármunn Súrsa. Táni was impressed by your efforts to purge the trolls from Urugarth and has sent you on another mission: to defeat Barashal, the leader of the Gertheryg.\n2\tTalk to Táni\tTáni is at Tármunn Súrsa, to the east of Carn Dûm. You defeated Barashal, the Lord of the Gertheryg, in battle and should return to Táni with the tidings of your success.\n",
[8149]="7002BFDF\n1\tDefeat brigands at Helstor (total: 10)\tBrigands can be found at Helstor, north of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola has asked you to defeat brigands at their encampment in the Brown Lands.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor. You should return to Céola with news of your success.\n",
[8150]="70025B35\n1\tInspect the crumbling seals (total: 4)\tTham Varan is east of Tinnudir and beyond Tham Nambarth. Gúrhebnir asked you to venture to Tham Varan and inspect several crumbling seals to determine the history of the ruins.\n2\tTalk to Gúrhebnir at Tinnudir\tThe Rangers are at Tinnudir, west of Tham Varan and Tham Nambarth. One of the Rangers will be interested to learn of the few lines you were able to read.\n",
[8151]="700304B2\n1\tDefeat the Easterling Overlords\tThe Woodyard is on the eastern side of Jóshkhin Orda in the Wold, to the north of North-torr. You should defeat the Easterling Overlords at the Woodyard.\n2\tDefeat Serka\030Defeat Ulugh\tThe Woodyard is on the eastern side of Jóshkhin Orda in the Wold, to the north of North-torr. You should defeat the Easterling Overlords at the Woodyard.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated those responsible for organizing this particular force of Easterling siege-craft intended for the attack on Floodwend.\n",
[8152]="7004AB9D\n1\tComplete Barad-dûr: Lore of the Past\tCandúr can be found in Udûn. You should talk Candúr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted Barad-dûr: Lore of the Past.\n",
[8153]="7000C618\n1\tSearch for the distressed hare\tThe hare's den lies along the cliff running along the south-west edge of the Circle of Blood. Radagast has asked you to coax a rabbit to safety, teaching you the importance of the bond with the gentler creatures of nature.\n2\tLead the hare back to Radagast\tRadagast is at Barad Dhorn in Agamaur. Radagast has asked you to coax a rabbit to safety, teaching you the importance of the bond with the gentler creatures of nature. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast the Brown is at Barad Dhorn. You have safely brought the Hare back to Radagast. You should speak to Radagast to see what else he might ask of you.\n",
[8154]="7000C619\n1\tSearch for the distressed sparrow\tThe sparrow's nest can be found amongst the ruins in the south-west of Harloeg, far to the south of Agamaur. Radagast the Brown has charged you with rescuing the sparrow of Haragmar.\n2\tBring the sparrow back to Radagast\tRadagast the Brown is at Barad Dhorn in Agamaur. You should quickly bring the sparrow back to Radagast before it gets scared and flies back to its nest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast the Brown is at Barad Dhorn. You should speak to Radagast to see what else he would have you do.\n",
[8155]="7000C61A\n1\tSearch for the distressed turtle\tThe turtle can be found hiding among fallen stones just to the east of the Circle of Blood. Radagast has asked you to coax the turtle to safety, teaching you the importance of the bond with the gentler creatures of nature.\n2\tBring the turtle back to Radagast\tRadagast the Brown is at Barad Dhorn in Agamaur. Radagast has asked you to coax a turtle to safety, teaching you the importance of the bond with the gentler creatures of nature. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast the Brown is at Barad Dhorn. You should find out if Radagast the Brown has anything else for you to do.\n",
[8156]="700174AE\n1\tTalk to Winiel at the Water-works\tWiniel is in the Water-works in Moria. You have been instructed to look for the lore-master Winiel.\n2\tTalk to Winiel at the Water-works\tWiniel is in the Water-works in Moria. You have been instructed to look for the lore-master Winiel.\n",
[8157]="700000AF\n1\tMeet Isdi for further Lore-master training\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, on the slopes above Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin. You have been told to speak with the lore-master Isdi, for she may have some wise words to share with you.\n2\tTalk to Isdi\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, on the slopes above Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin. You have been told to speak with the lore-master Isdi, for she may have some wise words to share with you.\n",
[8158]="70026C70\n1\tFind Skalli's shield\030Find Skalli's spear\030Find Skalli's mug\030Find Skalli's mining pick\030Find Skalli's lucky jewel\tSkalli's items have been flung all over the race area. You should consult the note he gave you for hints as to where the missing belongings might be. You should collect all of Skalli's missing items and return them to him.\n2\tBring the items to Skalli\tSkalli can be found at the Summer Festival Keg Race, likely still kicking the same waggon and cursing his luck (and festivals). You should bring Skalli his found belongings and attempt to cheer him up.\n",
[8159]="7003FDE6\n1\tTalk to Osbenn in Lancrath\tOsbenn can be found in the village of Lancrath, far to the south-east of Morlad. Rosfin has asked you to travel to the village of Lancrath and aid the people in repelling the Orcs of the White Mountains.\n",
[8160]="7000F023\n1\tBring the Lossoth spear-heads to Juha\030Collect Lossoth spear-heads (total: 10)\tJuha is at Sûri-kylä and Pynti-peldot in Forochel. Juha has asked you to bring him any Lossoth spear-heads which you find during your travels.\n",
})
